# Mesh beacon: the last ModuleConfig section, and the two shapes it needed.
#
# Filmed because both of them are about what a row *says* rather than what it does. The three
# flags are one word on the wire, so they are checkboxes: the question is which of these the
# beacon does, not whether each of three settings is on. And the four targets are one record
# repeated, so absent has to be a value a row can show - which is why every empty row in the
# section reads the same way rather than one of them saying "Unset" because that is what the
# region enum happens to call zero.
#
# The empty targets are the point of the last half. They are listed whether or not the radio
# sent one, exactly as an empty channel slot is, because an empty slot is how a target is added.

scene demo
scale 4
delay 200
config

tab settings
hold 400
# Down to Modules, into it, and down to Mesh beacon.
key down 12
hold 500
key a
hold 700
key down 12
hold 500
key a
hold 1400

# The three flags, which the fb backend draws as a set rather than as three switches.
key down 2
hold 1000

# Broadcast. The interval's presets start at the firmware's own floor of an hour and the slider
# is drawn over them, so one press right is a step on a scale rather than a number typed.
key down 1
hold 900
key right
hold 1200

# The invitation the beacon carries: a name and a key, which is a whole ChannelSettings on the
# wire and so the same two rows the Channels section draws.
key down 2
hold 900
key down 1
hold 1200

# Target 1, which names a preset and a channel of its own.
key down 3
hold 1000
key down 2
hold 1000

# And Target 2, which holds nothing. Three rows all reading the same way is what says the slot
# is empty rather than half filled in.
key down 1
hold 1600
